 You commanded. Thus, they suppressed the truth, deviated from the right path, aided the factions, distorted the Book, and disbelieved in the truth when it came to them. They held fast to falsehood when it confronted them, wasted Your right, led Your creation astray, and killed the children of Your Prophet, the elite of Your servants, the bearers of Your knowledge, and the inheritors of Your wisdom and Your revelation. O Allah, make the feet of Your enemies, the enemies of Your Messenger, and the enemies of the Household of Your Messenger tremble. O Allah, destroy their homelands, shatter their weapons, cause divergence in their words, break their strength, weaken their plots, strike them with Your decisive sword, pelt them with Your crushing stone, overwhelm them completely with affliction, suppress them thoroughly with punishment, and chastise them with an unprecedented chastisement. O Allah, seize them with years of hardship and exemplary punishments like those with which You destroyed Your enemies; indeed, You take vengeance upon the criminals. O Allah, indeed Your Sunnah is discarded, Your laws are suspended, and the progeny of Your Prophet are wandering aimlessly in the land. O Allah, assist the truth and its people, suppress falsehood and its people, favor us with salvation, guide us to faith, hasten our relief, and unite it with the relief of Your close friends. Instill love for us in their hearts, and make us an arriving delegation to them. O Allah, destroy whoever made the day of the killing of Your Prophet’s son and Your elite choice an Eid, welcoming it with joy and celebration. Seize the last of them just as You seized the first of them. O Allah, double the punishment and exemplary torment upon the oppressors of the Household of Your Prophet, and destroy their factions, their leaders, their defenders, and their entire group. O Allah, double Your blessings, Your mercy, and Your bounties upon the progeny of Your Prophet—the discarded, fearful, and abased progeny, the remnants of the pure, immaculate, and blessed tree. O Allah, elevate their word, make their proof triumphant, and remove from them the affliction, the adversity, the darkness of falsehoods, and the blindness. Firmly establish the hearts of their Shia and Your party upon obedience to You, their guardianship (Wilayah), their victory, and their allegiance. Assist them, grant them patience over injury sustained for Your sake, and make for them witnessed days and praised, auspicious times, in which their relief is near and their empowerment and victory become mandatory, just as You guaranteed for Your close friends in Your revealed Book, for You said—and Your word is the truth: \"Allah has promised those who have believed among you and done righteous deeds that He will surely grant them succession upon the earth just as He granted it to those before them and that He will surely establish for them [in authority] their religion which He has preferred for them and that He will surely substitute for them, after their fear, security, [for] they worship Me, not associating anything with Me.\" O Allah, remove their grief, O He besides Whom none possesses the power to remove distress! O One! O Unique! O Living! O All-Sustaining! And I, O my God, am Your servant who fears You, returns to You, asks of You, turns toward You, and seeks refuge in Your courtyard, knowing well that there is no refuge from You except in You. O Allah, accept my supplication, and hear, O my God, my open prayers and my secret invocations. Make me among those whose deeds You are pleased with, whose rituals You have accepted, and whom You have saved through Your mercy; indeed, You are the Almighty, the Generous. O Allah, send blessings first and last upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad; bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and have mercy on Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, with the most complete and excellent blessings, benedictions, and mercy You have ever bestowed upon Your Prophets, Your Messengers, Your angels, and the bearers of Your Throne—by virtue of 'there is no god but You'. O Allah, do not cause separation between me and Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, Your blessings be upon him and upon them. Make me, O my Master, among the Shia of Muhammad, Ali, Fatima, al-Hasan, al-Husayn, and their pure, chosen progeny. Grant me adherence to their rope, satisfaction with their path, and adoption of their way; indeed, You are All-Bountiful, Generous.\nNow go into prostration (Sajdah), keep either side of your face on the earth, one after the other, and say:\nيَا مَنْ يَحْكُمُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يُرِيْدُ اَنْتَ حَكَمْتَ فَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ مَحْمُوْدًا مَّشْكُوْرًا فَعَجِّلْ يَا مَوْلاَىَ فَرَجَهُمْ وَ فَرَجَنَابِهِمْ فَاِنَّكَ ضَمِنْتَ اِعْزَازَهُمْ بَعْدَ الذِّلَّةِ وَ تَكْثِيْرَهُمْ بَعْدَ الْقِلَّةِ وَ اِظْهَارَهُمْ بَعْدَ الْخُمُوْلِ يَا اَصْدَقَ الصَّادِقِيْنَ وَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ فَاَسْئَلُكَ يَا اِلٰهِىْ وَ سَيِّدِىْ مُتَضَرِّعًا اِلَيْكَ بِجُوْدِكَ وَ كَرَمِكَ بَسْطَ اَمَلِىْ وَ تَجَاوُزَ عَنِّىْ وَ قَبُوْلَ قَلِيْلِ عَمَلِىْ وَ كَثِيْرِهٖ وَ الزِّيَادَةَ فِىْ اَيَّامِىْ وَ تَبْلِيْغِىْ ذٰلِكَ الْمَشْهَدَ وَ اَنْ تَجْعَلَنِىْ مِمَّنْ يُدْعٰى فَيُجِيْبُ اِلٰى طَاعَتِهِمْ وَ مُوَالاَتِهِمْ وَ نَصْرِهِمْ وَ تُرِيَنِىْ ذٰلِكَ قَرِيْبًا سَرِيْعًا فِىْ عَافِيَةٍ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ.\nYAA MAN YAHKOMO MAA YASHAAA-O WA YAF-A’LO MAA YOREEDO ANTA HAKAMTA FALAKAL HAMDO MA MAHMOODAM MASHKOORAN FA-A’JJIL YAA MAWLAAYA FARAJAHUM WA FARAJANAA BEHIM FA-INNAKA ZAMINTA E-A'ZAAZAHUM BA'DAZ ZILLATE WA TAKSEERAHUM BA'DAL QILLATE WA IZHAARAHUM BA'DAL KHOMOOLE YAA ASDAQAS SAADEQEENA WA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA FA-AS-ALOKA YAA ELAAHEE WA SAYYEDEE MOTAZARRE-A'N ELAYKA BEJOODEKA WA KARAMEKA BASTA AMALEE WA TAJAAWOZA A'NNEE WA QABOOLA QALEELE A'MALEE WA KASEEREHI WAZ-ZEYAADATA FEE AYYAAMEE WA TABLEEGHEE ZAALEKAL MASH-HADA WA AN TAJ-A'LANEE MIMMAN YUD-A' FA-YOJEEBO ELAA TAA-A'TEHIM WA MOWAALAATEHIM WA NASREHIM WA TOREYANEE ZAALEKA QAREEBAN SAREE-A'N FEE A'AFEYATIN INNAKA A'LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN.\nO He Who judges whatever He wills and does whatever He intends! You have judged, so to You belongs all praise, praised and thanked. Therefore, O my Master, hasten their relief (Faraj) and our relief through them; for indeed, You guaranteed their honor after abasement, their multiplication after paucity, and their manifestation after obscurity—O Most Truthful of the truthful, and O Most Merciful of the merciful! So I ask You, O my God and my Master, pleading to You by Your bounty and Your generosity, to expand my hope, to overlook [my shortcomings], to accept the small amount of my deeds as well as the large, to extend my days, and to cause me to reach that witnessed day [of their return]. And [I ask] that You make me among those who are called and thus answer to their obedience, their allegiance, and their victory; and that You show me that day near and swift, in safety and well-being; indeed, You are Powerful over all things.\nRaise your head, look towards the sky and say:\nاَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ لاَ يَرْجُوْنَ اَيَّامَكَ فَاَعِذْنِىْ يَا اِلٰهِىْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ.\nA-O’OZO BEKA AN AKOONA MENAL LAZEENA LAA YARJOONA AYYAAMAKA FA-A-I’ZNEE YAA ELAAHEE BE-RAHMATEKA MIN ZAALEKA.\nI seek refuge in You from being among those who do not hope for Your Days; so protect me from that, O my God, through Your mercy.\n(8)\tOn the day of Ashura, before sunset, we share sorrow with the Holy Prophet, Ali Al-Murtaza, Fatemah Zahra and Hasan al-Mujtaba (peace be upon them all) and show our love and deep feelings of grief by reciting the following Ziyarat.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اٰدَمَ صِفْوَةِ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ نُوْحٍ نَبِىِّ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُوْسٰى كَلِيْمِ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عِيْسٰى رُوْحِ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُحَمَّدٍ حَبِيْبِ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عَلِىٍّ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَلِىِّ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ الْحَسَنِ الشَّهِيْدِ سِبْطِ رَسُوْلِ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ الْبَشِيْرِ النَّذِيْرِ وَابْنَ سَيِّدِ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَآءِ سَيِدَةِ نِسَآءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خِيَرَةَ اللهِ وَابْنَ خِيَرَتِهٖ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ثَارَ اللهِ وَابْنَ ثَارِهٖ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْوِتْرَ الْمَوْتُوْرُ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْاِمَامُ الْهَادِى الزَّكِىُّ وَ عَلٰى اَرْوَاحٍ حَلَّت بِفِنَآئِكَ وَ اَقَامَتْ فِىْ جِوَارِكَ وَ وَفَدَتْ مَعَ زُوَّارِكَ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ مِنِّىْ مَا بَقِيْتُ وَ بَقِىَ اللَّيْلُ وَ النَّهَارُ فَلَقَدْ عَظُمَتْ بِكَ الرَّزِيَّةُ وَجَلَّ الْمُصَابُ فِى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ فِى الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَفِىْ اَهْلِ السَّمٰوٰتِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ وَ فِى الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَفِىْ اَهْلِ السَّمٰوٰتِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ وَ فِىْ سُكَّانِ الْاَرْضِيْنَ فَاِنَّا لِلّٰهِ وَ اِنَّا اِلَيْهِ رٰجِعُوْنَ وَ صَلَوٰتُ اللهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهٗ وَ تَحِيَّاتُهٗ عَلَيْكَ وَ عَلٰى اٰبَآئِكَ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ الْمُنْتَجَبِيْنَ وَ عَلٰى ذَرَارِيْهِمُ الْهُدَاةِ الْمَهْدِيِّيْنَ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلاَىَ وَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَ عَلٰى رُوْحِكَ وَ عَلٰى اَرْوَاحِهِمْ وَ عَلٰى تُرْبَتِكَ وَ عَلٰى تُرْبَتِهِمْ اَللّٰهُمَّ لَقِّهِمْ رَحْمَةً وَّ رِضْوَانًا وَّ رَوْحًا وَّ رَيْحَانًا اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلاَىَ يَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ يَابْنَ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ وَابْنَ سَيِّدِ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ وَ يَابْنَ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَآءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا شَهِيْدُ يَابْنَ الشَّهِيْدِ يَا اَخَا الشَّهِيْدِ يَا اَبَا الشُّهَدَآءِ اَللّٰهُمَّ بَلِّغْهُ عَنِّىْ فِىْ هٰذِهِ السَّاعَةِ وَ فِىْ هٰذَا الْيَوْمِ وَ فِىْ هٰذَا الْوَقْتِ وَ فِىْ كُلِّ وَقْتٍ تَحِيَّةً كَثِيْرَةً وَّ سَلاَمًا سَلاَمُ اللهِ عَلَيْكَ وَ رَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهٗ يَا بْنَ سَيِّدِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ وَ عَلَى الْمُسْتَشْهَدِيْنَ مَعَكَ سَلاَمًا مُّتَّصِلاً مَّا تَّصَلَ اللَّيْلُ وَ النَّهَارُ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَى الْحُسَيْنِ ابْنِ عَلِىِّ نِالشَّهِيْدِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلٰى عَلَىِّ ابْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ الشَّهِيْدِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلٰى عَبَّاسِ ابْنِ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ الشَّهِيْدِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَى الشُّهَدَآءِ مِنْ وُّلْدِ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَى الشُّهَدَآءِ مِنْ وُّلْدِ الْحَسَنِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَى الشُّهَدَآءِ مِنْ وُّلْدِ الْحَسَنِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَى الشُّهَدَآءِ مِنْ وُّلْدِ الْحُسَيْنِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَى الشُّهَدَآءِ مِنْ وُّلْدِ جَعْفَرٍ وَّ عَقِيْلٍ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلٰى كُلِّ مُسْتَشْهِدٍ مَّعَهُمْ مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ بَلِّغْهُمْ عَنِّىْ تَحِيَّةً كَثِيْرَةً وَّ سَلاَمًا اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللهِ اَحْسَنَ اللهُ لَكَ الْعَزَآءَ فِىْ وَلَدِكَ الْحُسَيْنِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكِ يَا فَاطِمَةُ اَحْسَنَ اللهُ لَكَ الْعَزَآءَ فِىْ وَلَدِكِ الْحُسَيْنِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَحْسَنَ اللهُ لَكَ الْعَزَآءَ فِىْ وَلَدِكَ الْحُسَيْنِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَبَا مُحَمَّدٍ نِ الْحَسَنِ اَحْسَنَ اللهُ لَكَ الْعَزَآءَ فِىْ اَخِيْكَ الْحُسَيْنِ يَا مَوْلاَىَ يَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ اَنَا ضَيْفُ اللهِ وَ ضَيْفُكَ وَجَارُ اللهِ وَ جَارُكَ وَ لِكُلِّ ضَيْفٍ وَّ جَارٍ قِرًى وَّ قِرَاىَ فِىْ هٰذَا الْوَقْتِ اَنْ تَسْئَلَ اللهَ سُبْحَانَهٗ وَ تَعَالٰى اَنْ يَّرْزُقَنِىْ فَكَاكَ رَقَبَتِىْ مِنَ النَّارِ اِنَّهٗ سَمِيْعُ الدُّعَآءِ قَرِيْبٌ مُّجِيْبٌ.\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA AADAMA SIFWATIL LAAHE. ASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA NOOHIN NABIYYIL LAAHE. ASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA IBRAAHEEMA KHALILIL LAAHE. ASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA MOOSAA KALEEMIL LAAHE. ASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA E’ESAA ROOHIL LAAHE. ASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA MOHAMMADIN HABEEBIL LAAHE. ASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA A’LIYYIN AMEERIL MOA-MENEENA WALIYYIL LAAHE. ASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESAL HASANISH SHAHEEDE SIBTE RASOOLIL LAAHE. ASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA RASOOLIL LAAHE ASSALAAO A’LAYKA YABNAL BASHEERIN NAZEERE WABNA SAYYEDIL WA